Title: "What Is Not Checked"
Id: "04cad904-1fb8-47c4-9ea6-01b11666ef8e"

Text: "MathLingua's checker does not prove theorem conclusions or verify that axioms and definitions are mathematically true.

A theorem conclusion is checked for syntax, command references, declared symbols, and local requirements, but not for semantic consequence from the assumptions.

The checker also does not infer arbitrary mathematics. If a command requires a
fact, that fact must be directly available from declarations, extensions,
capabilities, builds, views, or the limited reductions implemented by the
checker.

For example, knowing `A is \set` does not automatically establish every theorem about sets. Authors must encode the requirements and capabilities that a command needs, and the checker only follows those implemented rules."
Id: "c19f70b5-5c8d-4cdb-9b87-de4feaea917f"
